From df30a7b695d0ef4bd0f7d240d61a53e15d82aa36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:05:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] diag(wlan): count RX HIF, reorder and delivery events

Sustained downlink stalls for seconds while ping works, ss shows about
half the TCP segments arriving out of order, and the reorder miss
timeout from 0001 never fires. Nothing in the driver says where frames
wait or get reordered.

Count, in the driver main thread, what happens to every received
frame and print a summary every two seconds while frames arrive:

  ECHO_WLAN_RXSTAT: hif ...  enhanced status reads, status reads that
      report RX lengths with no RX DONE bit (nicProcessIST_impl()
      ignores those), port reads and frames per read, frames left in
      the port for lack of SW_RFBs, >16 or truncated, HIF header length
      vs status length mismatches, QM low-RFB drops.
  ECHO_WLAN_RXSTAT: ba ...   frames entering reordering, fall-within,
      arrivals that left frames behind a hole, fall-ahead and BAR
      window moves with the sequence numbers they gave up, fall-behind
      retries dropped / frames passed up out of order, duplicates,
      miss-timeout skips, longest wait in a reorder queue and frames
      that waited >= 100 ms, deepest queue, unicast data frames without
      the reorder flag.
  ECHO_WLAN_RXSTAT: ind ...  delivery batches, batches delivered on a
      different CPU than the previous one, and batches delivered while
      that CPU's ksoftirqd was runnable (netif_rx() then defers NET_RX
      to it, so frames from consecutive batches can reach TCP out of
      order).

Each anomaly also logs a rate-limited ECHO_WLAN_RXHIF / ECHO_WLAN_RX_BA
line. The summary timer arms on the first call because jiffies starts
just below its wrap. No behaviour change.
